{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794238077,"nonce":"eqYJNUHrof30sQfvkbM4zcaZs8M=","title":"The N1E incident surface term enters b with the opposite sign of every other trial-free term","message":"A trial-free volume term enters as b = -term (the term list sums to zero: inner(u,v) - inner(f,v) solves u = f). The N1E incident surface term inner(g, v x n) matched by the surface-load pattern enters as b = +term (residual = spatial_res(u) - nat_load), so it has right-hand-side semantics.\n\nConsequence: writing the incident load from the weak form with all terms on one side gives the field with the wrong sign. With the exact face operator on both faces and the derived load +2 i k_q einc_t . v_t, the field is -1 times the Fresnel field (relative error 1.97); negating the load gives 5.6 % (degree 2, about 3 cells per wavelength in the dielectric). The same integrand routed through the general boundary path would take the other sign.","files":null}]}